 "comments": [
  {
   "id": "858b41f9-7ffe-4d33-89d4-bc9e8f4c7174",
   "build_id": "375352af-1aad-4400-84fd-780eb62fd919",
   "author_id": "91ccb5a3-0946-49b1-a7e8-72512e09c6fb",
   "parent_id": null,
   "body": "So the only suggestion I have is to re-think your AoE rotation. Righteous Tempest is a trap. It should only be used in the rare scenario where you cannot titan strike or argent blade before your oath chain will run out. Instead, get 5+ stacks of cleave, and as many lunge stacks as you can while spaming argent blade/scarlet hammer and titan strike as much as possible. Don't wait for procs for Argent blade, just keep spamming it to do massive AoE with cleave stacks and maintain the oath chain as long as possible. No downtime just wall to wall pull and never stop. With a good tank you can keep going with 20-30 lunge stacks and 10 cleave stacks.",
   "upvotes": 2,
